It bundles one third-party file under a different license:

  models/embedding_b0.onnx … embedding_b5.onnx
    A speech embedding model published by Google as the TensorFlow Hub module
    "google/speech_embedding/1", described in:

      James Lin, Kevin Kilgour, Dominik Roblek, Matthew Sharifi.
      "Training Keyword Spotters with Limited and Synthesized Speech Data", 2020.
      https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.01322

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-embedding_model).
    The ONNX conversion of the module is the one distributed by the openWakeWord
    project (https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord), whose code is likewise
    Apache-2.0. The WakeWord project split that graph into six sub-graphs at its
    pooling layers so the model can run incrementally; no weight was changed.

The log-mel front end (Melspectrogram.cs) is an independent implementation of a
fixed signal-processing transform and is covered by this package's MIT license.
No pre-trained wake word models from openWakeWord are included.
